---
const consequences = [
  {
    title: 'No horizontal scaling',
    body: 'Total capacity is whatever one node can ingest and validate. Adding validators spreads storage and execution around, and the ceiling stays exactly where it was.',
    note: 'Validators added → ceiling unchanged',
  },
  {
    title: 'It halts rather than fork',
    body: 'Under a network partition the system is CP. It stops instead of risking a rollback, so a global partition can take the cloud down until it heals.',
    note: 'Partition → stop, never diverge',
  },
];
---

<section class="band band--tint" id="cost">
  <div class="field" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="orb"></span>
    <span class="orb orb--low"></span>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap reveal">
    <div class="split">
      <h2>The part we don't hide.</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Holding both guarantees requires a single global DAG with one total order. Every
          operation, from every app, passes through it and is seen by every validator, even
          though each validator only stores and executes a fraction of the state.
        </p>
        <p>Two things follow from that, and both are load-bearing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Numbered because the sentence above counts them: two, in order. -->
    <ol class="costs">
      {
        consequences.map((item, index) => (
          <li class="cost">
            <p class="num">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</p>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="body">{item.body}</p>
            <p class="note">{item.note}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <p class="closer">
      The bet that makes this worth taking is bandwidth. Per-node bandwidth keeps climbing,
      and putting only hashes on the consensus path, with the data available elsewhere,
      makes that bet easier to win while the total order stays whole.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* The band dissolves at both edges, so the bodies inside it have to dissolve
     with it. Without the mask they stop dead on the section boundary and the
     seam is the first thing the eye finds. */
  .field {
    mask-image: linear-gradient(
      to bottom,
      transparent 0%,
      #000 14%,
      #000 86%,
      transparent 100%
    );
  }

  /* Bleeding off the left, where the hero's runs off the right, so the two
     read as the same body seen from opposite sides of the page. Both stay far
     enough out that their dense centres never sit under a line of text.

     Retuned to ash and linen: the band already carries a colour, and wine is
     already spoken for by the numbers and the readouts. */
  .orb {
    --spin: 128deg;
    --c1: #9eb09b;
    --c2: #b3c1b0;
    --c3: #cfd6c8;
    --c4: #efe6dc;

    top: -34vw;
    left: -42vw;
    width: 68vw;
    aspect-ratio: 1;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  .orb--low {
    --spin: 292deg;

    top: auto;
    bottom: -26vw;
    left: auto;
    right: -22vw;
    width: 48vw;
    opacity: 0.7;
    animation-duration: 61s;
    animation-direction: alternate-reverse;
  }

  .costs {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 8rem) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  /* Staggered on purpose. Two landings the reader arrives at one after the
     other, not two cells of a table read at once. */
  .cost {
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-tint);
  }

  .cost:first-child {
    grid-column: 1 / span 5;
  }

  .cost:last-child {
    grid-column: 7 / span 6;
    margin-top: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .num {
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5.5rem);
    font-weight: 200;
    line-height: 0.8;
    letter-spacing: -0.06em;
    color: var(--wine);
  }

  .cost h3 {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.9rem;
  }

  .body {
    max-width: 40ch;
    color: var(--ink-tint);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .note {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--step-meta);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--wine);
  }

  .closer {
    max-width: 34ch;
    margin-top: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-tint);
    font-size: var(--step-lede);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-tint);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .costs {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 3rem;
    }

    .cost:first-child,
    .cost:last-child {
      grid-column: 1;
      margin-top: 0;
    }

    .body,
    .closer {
      max-width: none;
    }
  }
</style>
